{"name":"Intellectual","hex":"#3f414c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"intellectual","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Pertaining to, or performed by, the intellect; mental or cognitive.","Endowed with intellect; having a keen sense of understanding; having the capacity for higher forms of knowledge or thought; characterized by intelligence or cleverness"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An intelligent, learned person, especially one who discourses about learned matters.","The intellect or understanding; mental powers or faculties."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intellectual"}],"entries":[{"title":"Intellectual","blocks":[{"text":"An intellectual is a person who engages in critical thinking, research, and reflection about the nature of reality, especially the nature of society and proposed solutions for its normative problems. Coming from the world of culture, either as a creator or as a mediator, the intellectual participates in politics, either to defend a concrete proposition or to denounce an injustice, usually by either rejecting, producing or extending an ideology, and by defending a system of values."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Intellectual","wikidata":"Q58968"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/J%E2%80%99accuse.jpg/500px-J%E2%80%99accuse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/J%E2%80%99accuse.jpg/1280px-J%E2%80%99accuse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/J%E2%80%99accuse.jpg/500px-J%E2%80%99accuse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The front page of L'Aurore (13 January 1898) featured Émile Zola's open letter J'Accuse…! asking the French President Félix Faure to resolve the Dreyfus affair.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJ%E2%80%99accuse.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Edwards_Amasa_Park.jpg/500px-Edwards_Amasa_Park.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Edwards_Amasa_Park.jpg/500px-Edwards_Amasa_Park.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Congregational theologian Edwards Amasa Park proposed segregating the intellectuals from the public sphere of society in the United States.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEdwards_Amasa_Park.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Portrait_of_Milton_Friedman.jpg/500px-Portrait_of_Milton_Friedman.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Portrait_of_Milton_Friedman.jpg/1280px-Portrait_of_Milton_Friedman.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Portrait_of_Milton_Friedman.jpg/500px-Portrait_of_Milton_Friedman.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The economist Milton Friedman identified the intelligentsia and the business class as interfering with capitalism.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APortrait_of_Milton_Friedman.jpg"}],"sounds":{"intellectual":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/78/En-us-intellectual.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/7/78/En-us-intellectual.ogg/En-us-intellectual.ogg.mp3"}]},"pictures":[{"title":"WIPO Director General Speaks at Launch Ceremony for Egypt’s National Intellectual Property Strategy","image":"https://thumb.wiki